\begin{align*}
4u - 5v &= 23 \quad \text{(1)} \\
2u + 4v &= -8 \quad \text{(2)}
\end{align*}
First, we can multiply equation (2) by 2 to make the coefficients of $u$ the same in both equations:
\begin{align*}
2(2u + 4v) &= 2(-8) \\
4u + 8v &= -16 \quad \text{(3)}
\end{align*}
Now, we can subtract equation (3) from equation (1) to eliminate $u$:
\begin{align*}
(4u - 5v) - (4u + 8v) &= 23 - (-16) \\
4u - 5v - 4u - 8v &= 39 \\
-13v &= 39 \\
v &= -3
\end{align*}
Now that we have the value of $v$, we can substitute it back into equation (2) to solve for $u$:
\begin{align*}
2u + 4(-3) &= -8 \\
2u - 12 &= -8 \\
2u &= 4 \\
u &= 2
\end{align*}
Finally, we can find the value of $u+v$:
\begin{align*}
u + v &= 2 + (-3) \\
u + v &= -1
\end{align*}
Therefore, the value of $u+v$ is $\boxed{-1}$.

